or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; April fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Tri-Cities' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.03 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 7.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1948 (12.90 in); the driest, 1967 (3.78 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, no daily record lows"}}